diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..89fb988 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,20 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Receiving events
+
+When a subscribed event occurs, Fizzy queues a JSON `POST` to each active webhook on that board. The body contains the event's `id`, `action`, `created_at`, and action-specific `particulars`, plus the `eventable` (a card or comment), `board`, and `creator` in their API formats. Slack and Campfire URLs receive a chat message instead. Configure `BASE_URL` on self-hosted instances so links in the payload point to your instance.
+
+Each request includes:
+
+- `X-Webhook-Delivery-ID`: a unique ID for this webhook's delivery of the event.
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: the UTC time of the attempt in ISO 8601 format.
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: the hexadecimal HMAC-SHA256 of the **raw request body**, keyed with the webhook's signing secret. Verify it before processing the payload.
+
+Fizzy makes at most one POST attempt per webhook and event, even if the delivery job is replayed. It does not retry timeouts or follow redirects. A timeout or worker interruption is not proof that the receiver did not process the event.
+
+A `2xx` response counts as success and resets the failure streak. A webhook is disabled when it has at least ten consecutive failures and an hour or more has elapsed since the first failure in that streak. Reactivating it resets the streak and resumes deliveries for new events. Delivery history is retained for up to one week.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
